1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,495
On Tempo, MPP lets agents and apps pay per request

2
00:00:04,545 --> 00:00:08,586
— including paying for an answer before they send money.

3
00:00:08,636 --> 00:00:11,768
"Will this payment actually reach the receiver?"

4
00:00:11,818 --> 00:00:13,586
is worth paying for.

5
00:00:13,636 --> 00:00:19,950
But today, if that answer is wrong, MPP leaves the refund to the server.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,037
On Tempo, a transfer can succeed while the receiver gets nothing:

7
00:00:25,088 --> 00:00:28,737
receive policies send it to a guard instead.

8
00:00:28,787 --> 00:00:32,900
Policies, fee tokens and balances all change the outcome

9
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:38,450
— so a good answer is valuable, and a wrong one is costly.

10
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,593
Sworn lets the seller back its answer with money.

11
00:00:42,643 --> 00:00:46,736
The agent buys an answer about the current block;

12
00:00:46,786 --> 00:00:51,799
the seller locks part of its bond behind exactly that answer.

13
00:00:51,849 --> 00:00:57,783
If it's false, anyone can prove it, and the bond pays the agent.

14
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:01,926
The agent gets an answer it can rely on;

15
00:01:01,976 --> 00:01:05,609
the seller gets proof it can be trusted.

16
00:01:05,659 --> 00:01:07,450
No judge, no owner.

17
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,228
It's built from Tempo's own parts.

18
00:01:10,278 --> 00:01:15,320
Tempo's Zones work already re-runs Tempo's EVM against a proven state

19
00:01:15,370 --> 00:01:17,635
— Tempo needs this primitive too.

20
00:01:17,685 --> 00:01:24,117
I took it into a zero-knowledge proof: tempo-revm, proven against Tempo's own block hash.

21
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:27,820
It matched forty of forty real Moderato transfers,

22
00:01:27,870 --> 00:01:32,450
and on Moderato it has already slashed a lying server.

23
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:37,583
I build on Reth and Revm; I teach them in rethlab.

24
00:01:37,633 --> 00:01:43,183
Next: a bonded-answer method any MPP seller on Tempo can switch on.

25
00:01:43,233 --> 00:01:46,450
Sworn — answers you can hold to account.
